# REBASH Academy Tutorial Page System

## Canonical format (mandatory)

Body structure and quality bar:

- `.cursor/prompts/tutorial-format-linux.md` (all technologies)
- `.cursor/rules/00-foundation/09-content-quality-standard.mdc`
- `.cursor/prompts/CONTENT_QUALITY.md`

Hands-on Lab: topic-specific, copy-paste executable, full subsection list (Objective → Cleanup). No note-taking labs.  
Interview Questions: 5–8 topic-specific + 2–3 sample answers.  
Diagrams: Excalidraw only (never D2/Mermaid for tutorials).

Prefer Codex for content generation until the user changes agents.

## Purpose

This rule defines how tutorial pages should be generated.

A tutorial teaches learners how to accomplish one specific goal through guided, hands-on practice.

Tutorials should always be outcome-driven.

Learners should finish with a working result.

